WEBVTT

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:06.241
It's Monday morning, and Mai already has over a hundred

00:00:06.241 --> 00:00:08.505
and fifty CVs for one open role.

00:00:08.505 --> 00:00:13.581
InterviewPath's AI has screened every CV against her real hiring criteria

00:00:13.581 --> 00:00:16.325
and sorted them onto an evidence board.

00:00:16.325 --> 00:00:21.264
The Priority lane holds strong matches, backed up by strong interviews.

00:00:21.264 --> 00:00:25.859
But look at Hidden Gem — candidates whose paper resume looks thin,

00:00:25.859 --> 00:00:29.083
yet whose spoken answers showed real evidence.

00:00:29.083 --> 00:00:32.856
A plain CV filter would have missed every one of them.

00:00:33.156 --> 00:00:35.449
A new role opens on her team.

00:00:35.449 --> 00:00:38.200
Instead of staring at a blank page,

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:43.168
InterviewPath's AI drafts a complete job description in minutes,

00:00:43.168 --> 00:00:47.066
pulled straight from her company's real standards,

00:00:47.066 --> 00:00:52.645
with the must-have criteria and the sourcing channels already tagged for

00:00:52.645 --> 00:00:53.868
tracking later.

00:00:54.168 --> 00:00:59.929
InterviewPath's Channel Intelligence breaks down every application by source

00:00:59.929 --> 00:01:03.595
— LinkedIn, TopCV, university fairs, referrals —

00:01:03.595 --> 00:01:09.057
and shows exactly which channel brings candidates she actually approves,

00:01:09.057 --> 00:01:10.778
not just the most CVs.

00:01:10.778 --> 00:01:15.716
So instead of spending the biggest budget on the loudest channel,

00:01:15.716 --> 00:01:19.831
she spends it on the one with the lowest cost per real

00:01:19.831 --> 00:01:20.280
hire.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:24.542
Employees stop pinging HR for every small question.

00:01:24.542 --> 00:01:30.332
They ask InterviewPath's Copilot directly, and it answers straight from the

00:01:30.332 --> 00:01:33.608
real company handbook, citing its sources.

00:01:33.608 --> 00:01:37.569
It even catches when two policy documents disagree,

00:01:37.569 --> 00:01:43.131
flagging the conflict instead of guessing. Screening. Writing. Channels.

00:01:43.131 --> 00:01:43.740
Policy.

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:48.540
One AI platform, built around how your company actually hires.
